# <Customer> connections (no secrets)

Connection details and passwords live in `C:\passwords\<client>-connections.txt`
on MarchHare. Never copy them into this repo, a commit, a PR, a log or a chat.
Never dump that file to stdout or to agent tool logs, even when intending to
print only keys for redaction. Read it into variables only; print lengths or
boolean found flags. If a secret hits a log, stop and tell the operator
immediately.

Source connection data from the authorized Priority customer connections
subform (`ZEMG_CUSTCONECT_SUBFORM` / `ZEMG_CUSTCONECTD_SUBFORM`) when needed.

## Primary agent route: airc console

When an airc console exists (for example `<HOST>_console`), it is the primary
agent route. Record the console name, machine id and any verified read-only
findings here. Live writes still need explicit approval.

## Human route: AnyDesk or TeamViewer

Record addresses or IDs and named Windows / Tabula users. Do not record
passwords.

## Fallback: web

Record environment URLs. Note when a URL is only reachable from inside the
customer network.

